Z||000000||ichifiero||08-18-2001||08:16 PM||||I am still wuite interested in doing a 4.5L cadillac swap. How many hours should I expect to complete this project? I am pretty mechanically inclined (having built over 100 airplanes). Since my fiero is my daily driver, I need to know how much time  to plan for.<BR>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||08-18-2001||10:19 PM||||The 4.5 goes into the Fiero really easily. If you're not using the trans that's in the Fiero, get a spare cradle to set up the new drivetrain on. There's a lot you can do before you even toch the Fiero. That will save on downtime. Getting the engine in the car only takes a few hours, but hooking everything up and sorting out the wiring will take a while. The exhaust system will also take some time depending on what you choose to do. If you have all the parts on hand and know exactly what you'r doing, I'd plan on having the car down for at least a week. Personally I'd find another car to drive before starting the project. I just don't like to be rushing to get things done. Have fun!||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||08-18-2001||11:42 PM||||well im going to attemp to bolt my cradle with Caddy Trans/Engine in tommrow... I have spent countless hours working on my conversion, but then i am doing in on my spare time, by myself, with no money (no job), and im 15   Ill post some pix or something<P>Kyle||||reg||1
